The conversation revolved around a recommendation letter for Mohammad Taky Tahmid, a PhD student at the University of Delaware, applying for the David H. Smith Conservation Research Fellowship. Key prompts included outlining the student’s proposed research project on landowner incentives for conserving tidal marshes in Delaware and highlighting his qualifications. The responses emphasized Tahmid's intellectual independence and capacity to identify significant research questions across climate, agriculture, and labor economics. Suggestions for improving the letter included tightening language, correcting phrasing errors, and enhancing clarity and evaluative strength. The conclusion was revised to specifically reflect the fellowship's goals, asserting Tahmid’s suitability for the program based on his innovative research and collaborative approach.
